config.h started as a copy of config.def.h. Edit config.h; keep
config.def.h as upstream so new releases can be compared against it.

Patches (originals from tools.suckless.org/dmenu/patches, kept in
patches/, applied in this order; dmenu.c already has them, so don't
apply again):
  center             dmenu-center-20250407-b1e217b.diff
  bordercolor        dmenu-bordercolor-20230512-0fe460d.diff
  fuzzymatch         dmenu-fuzzymatch-5.3.diff
  fuzzyhighlight     dmenu-fuzzyhighlight-5.3.diff
                     (scheme enum and usage() by hand)
  sort_by_popularity dmenu-sort_by_popularity-20250117-86f0b51.diff
                     (reworked by hand: only with the new -P flag, so
                     other scripts piping into dmenu don't fill the
                     cache; items are sorted once at start and keep the
                     upstream exact/prefix/substring order instead of
                     having their text swapped; with fuzzy matching the
                     order is exact match, starts with the first letter
                     typed, popularity, then closeness of the match;
                     Shift+Return (typed text) isn't counted)
  navhistory+search  dmenu-navhistory+search-20250328-52fc8a0.diff
                     (rewritten by hand: Up/Down instead of Alt+p/n walk
                     the -H history, searching by what was typed before
                     the first Up; Ctrl+p/n still move in the list; a
                     repeated choice moves to the newest place instead of
                     being dropped; no Ctrl+r and no dmenu_run change)
Their config.def.h hunks are not applied (config.def.h stays upstream);
the settings are in config.h. usage() and dmenu.1 also list -c, -bw, -P, -H.

dmenu_apps and apps are ours: Mod+p in dwm runs dmenu_apps, which shows
only the programs in apps (linked to ~/.config/dmenu/apps by install.sh).
